course: dictionary
lesson: 11148
title: Wildfire: fire that spreads
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A wildfire is a big fire that spreads out of control through forests, bush or grassland. The sentence «Wildfires and bushfires move very fast, especially with wind» gives you clues: move very fast and wind tell you it is a fast, dangerous fire. Always check by swapping in your meaning.
explain: The word also has a second meaning. «Spread like wildfire» means spread very quickly, like news or a rumour. Try it: if someone says the news spread like wildfire, the news went around very fast, not that it was on fire.
explain: Other clues help too. «When there is a wildfire evacuation order, leave early with your family» tells you a wildfire is dangerous enough that you must leave home. Wildfires are called bushfires in Australia and New Zealand, and forest fires or brush fires in North America.
fact: A wildfire is a big fire that spreads out of control through forests, bush or grassland.
fact: Wildfires spread fast in hot, dry, windy weather: dry plants are fuel, and wind brings fresh oxygen.
fact: Lightning, campfires, sparks, cigarettes and arson can all start a wildfire.
fact: «Spread like wildfire» means spread very quickly, like news or a rumour.
fact: When there is a fire ban, do not light any fire at all, because one spark can start a wildfire.
exercise: «Wildfires and bushfires move very fast, especially with wind.» What is a wildfire? | A fire that is put out on purpose | A cold wind that blows across the hills | A small, tidy fire in a fireplace | *A big fire that spreads out of control through forests, bush or grassland
exercise: Priya says, «The news spread like wildfire through the school.» What does this mean? | The news caught fire in the kitchen | The news was very long | The news was written down in ink | *The news spread very quickly
exercise: «Wildfires spread fast in dry, hot, windy weather.» Find and copy one word that means quick. | wind | wildfires | weather | *fast
test: «When there is a wildfire evacuation order, leave early with your family and never go back for toys.» What should you do? | Go back for your toys first | *Leave early with your family and do not go back for toys | Wait until the road is blocked | Stay home and light a candle
test: When there is a fire ban, what can one spark cause? | A rainbow after the rain | A snowfall on the hills | *A wildfire | A cooler, calmer day
exam: Which is the best meaning of «spread like wildfire»? | *Spread very quickly, like news or a rumour | Spread slowly under the ground | Burn the forest down slowly | Glow in the dark like a lamp
